# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tozed P11IDU - network defaults
#
# Author: Nipun Methmal
#
# Insert into:  target/linux/ramips/mt76x8/base-files/etc/board.d/02_network
# Indentation:  TABS - 1 tab for the case arm, 2 tabs for the body,
#               3 tabs for continuation lines.
#
# Both arms below were read back verbatim from a running P11IDU
# (/etc/board.d/02_network, the tozed,p11idu arms of ramips_setup_interfaces
# and ramips_setup_macs) and are reproduced unchanged. The switch port roles
# were cross-checked against /proc/mtd, the decompiled device tree and
# docs/01-hardware-and-attack-surface.md:
#
#     port 0, 1, 3  ->  LAN   (VLAN 1 untagged, CPU port 6 tagged)
#     port 2, 4     ->  WAN   (VLAN 2 untagged, CPU port 6 tagged)
#     port 6        ->  CPU
#
# Only the LAN side is brought up by default; the wired WAN belongs to an
# outdoor unit that is not part of this bundle.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ===========================================================================
# (1) ramips_setup_interfaces()
#
# Suggested insertion point: immediately after the teltonika,rut241 arm,
# before hiwifi,hc5761a. The running unit carries it after widora,neo-32m
# instead - the ordering inside a `case` is not significant.
#
#     tozed,p11idu)
#             ucidef_add_switch "switch0" \
#                     "0:lan" "1:lan" "3:lan" "2:wan" "4:wan" "6@eth0"
#             ;;
#
# ===========================================================================
# (2) ramips_setup_macs()
#
# Suggested insertion point: immediately before the tplink,archer-c20-v4
# arm - the same position the running unit carries it in.
#
#     tozed,p11idu)
#             lan_mac=$(mtd_get_mac_binary factory 0x28)
#             wan_mac=$(macaddr_add "$lan_mac" 1)
#             ;;
#
# factory + 0x28 is the WAN/LAN base MAC cell described by the `macaddr@28`
# nvmem cell in the device tree; the second address is simply base + 1.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The two blocks below are the copy-paste payload, kept tab-indented:

# ---8<--- ramips_setup_interfaces: tozed,p11idu ---
	tozed,p11idu)
		ucidef_add_switch "switch0" \
			"0:lan" "1:lan" "3:lan" "2:wan" "4:wan" "6@eth0"
		;;
# ---8<--- /ramips_setup_interfaces ---

# ---8<--- ramips_setup_macs: tozed,p11idu ---
	tozed,p11idu)
		lan_mac=$(mtd_get_mac_binary factory 0x28)
		wan_mac=$(macaddr_add "$lan_mac" 1)
		;;
# ---8<--- /ramips_setup_macs ---
